Summary of the Construction
To summarize, the construction consists of:
• An ideal triangulation X of M;
• A balanced angle structure θ: X3,1 →C;
• State variables x ∈AX2, dynamical variables z ∈AX3;
35
• The kinematical kernel KX(y, z);
• The dynamical weight DX,θ(z);
• The final integral yielding FR,X,θ(y).
The analytic convergence, Pachner invariance, and angle gauge invariance of this
integral will be elucidated systematically in the chapters to follow.
36
CHAPTER 5

Conceptual Summary
The angle-deformed state-integral formalism upholds a mathematically rigorous
topological invariant by combining:
• Triangulation combinatorics, captured via Pachner moves;
• Angle structures, encoding geometric deformation parameters;
• Quantum harmonic analysis over Gaussian groups;
• Functional identities of the quantum dilogarithm Ψa,c;
• Tempered distribution theory, ensuring analytic well-definedness.
This framework realizes a quantized version of decorated Teichm¨uller theory and
connects to Chern–Simons theory, TQFTs, and arithmetic quantum topology over
both Archime
